      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WAH ELM (5) was big odds last time but gave a huge sight after a fast early split, grabbed late but holding on to a placing when a 4.5 lengths third (26.07) over 450m at Ballarat. Some good form is emerging from her last run. Can go on with it. WAH CEDAR (7) turned spotting a big start finishing fifth (26.26) last time in a Maiden at Ballarat. Deserves plenty of respect. PAW CAMPUS (4) still a maiden after six runs but rarely out of the placings. Is better than last start when out of the placings, finishing fifth (23.47) at Geelong. Must be included in calculations. OSCAR MIKE (8) is a James Shaw-trained newcomer by Fernando Bale out of Big Suzie. Start all important and will need some luck getting across from the wide draw. Expected to produce a bold debut.",
